lma (1.3.0-0ubuntu1) jammy; urgency=medium

  * Optional NUMA memory binding per allocation (AllowedMemoryNodes=):
    interactive step with live preview (latency, free memory on the node,
    OOM warning, other users bound there), --mem local|any flag, and config
    "memoryBinding": off | optional | local-by-default. Preselected for
    sockets with a GPU; never applied silently unless local-by-default.
  * Allocation database gains a "mems" column (older files still load);
    hooks receive the NUMA node list as a 5th argument.
  * Setup wizard asks about memory binding; status shows each binding.

 -- Meetesh K Mehta <meeteshmehta4@gmail.com>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 09:17:14 +0000

lma (1.2.0-0ubuntu1) jammy; urgency=medium

  * Compact / spread placement over CCDs: --compact, --spread, --ccds N and
    config "placement". Spread keeps both hyperthreads of every core together
    and prefers CCDs no other user is on.
  * Layout menu organised by workload ("Cache / latency-sensitive" vs
    "Memory-bound"); duplicate layouts are hidden.
  * Live preview while choosing: CCD strip of the socket plus implications
    (memory bandwidth in CCD links, cache locality, L3 size and sharing).
  * Allocation summary shows the CCD strip and implications.
  * Setup wizard asks for the shared region in physical cores and how to split
    it across sockets, instead of a CPU list.
  * Core map shows CCD boundaries; version shown in the banner.

 -- Meetesh K Mehta <meeteshmehta4@gmail.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 21:23:11 +0000

lma (1.1.0-0ubuntu1) jammy; urgency=medium

  * Socket-aware allocation (interactive picker and --socket), GPU locality shown per socket.
  * cpulist support in config (e.g. "0-7,128-135"), optional allocationUnit logical|physical.
  * Interactive arrow-key UI with core map; non-interactive --size/--release/--status flags.
  * lma-setup wizard when no config is given; config stored in /etc/lma/config.json; --check.
  * Fix irqaffinity written as a Python list in GRUB config.
  * Fix stale per-user drop-ins surviving re-setup; per-operation locking; safer sudoers write.
  * Stop deleting unrelated systemd drop-ins in setup, reset and postrm.

 -- Meetesh K Mehta <meeteshmehta4@gmail.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

